{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f5f6f1e972ded0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9006: Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Major.\n13\t\n14\tThe strategy brings upstream Feast in as a supported, installable RHOAI component.\n15\tFeast has a reserved Jira component (Feature Store) but no productized repository,\n16\tno build pipeline, and no operator integration — it is a **new component** (no\n17\tarchitecture context file exists for it), so the full onboarding chain is generated\n18\t(Rule 20). The single open question — which deployment topology to productize\n19\tfirst (operator-based vs. standalone server per project) — has two bounded\n20\toutcomes and changes which deployment/enablement epics exist, so it is a gating\n21\tInvestigation with conditional decomposition branches.\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List\n24\t\n25\tMain plan:\n26\t\n27\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n28\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Select and validate the Feast productization deployment topology | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Midstream Feast repository onboarding under opendatahub-io | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Konflux onboarding for the Feature Store build pipeline | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Feast SDK preinstalled in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Dashboard presence and endpoint links for the Feature Store | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-E007 | Feature Store documentation: enablement, getting started, supported limits | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n36\t\n37\tConditional branches (not standalone Jira issues; attached to the gating\n38\tInvestigation as a plan document):\n39\t\n40\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n41\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E008 | Productize the operator-based Feast deployment (Branch A) | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 | Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, operator topology (Branch A) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E008 | Productize the standalone per-project Feast server (Branch B) | Implementation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009 | Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, standalone topology (Branch B) | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n46\t\n47\t`epic_count` = 11 (7 main-plan epics + 4 branch epics). Main-plan critical path\n48\tlength = 3 (e.g., license-validation → workbench SDK image → documentation;\n49\tequally, topology decision → Dashboard integration → documentation, and in each\n50\tbranch: topology decision → deployment → Platform Operator enablement).\n51\t\n52\t## Dependency DAG\n53\t\n54\t```mermaid\n55\tgraph TD\n56\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: topology decision\"]\n57\t    E002[\"E002 repo-onboarding\"]\n58\t    E003[\"E003 license-validation\"]\n59\t    E004[\"E004 konflux-onboarding\"]\n60\t    E005[\"E005 workbench Feast SDK image\"]\n61\t    E006[\"E006 Dashboard integration\"]\n62\t    E007[\"E007 documentation\"]\n63\t    A008[\"Branch A E008: operator-based deployment\"]\n64\t    A009[\"Branch A E009: Platform Operator enablement (operator)\"]\n65\t    B008[\"Branch B E008: standalone per-project server\"]\n66\t    B009[\"Branch B E009: Platform Operator enablement (standalone)\"]\n67\t\n68\t    E002 --> E004\n69\t    E003 --> E005\n70\t    E001 --> E006\n71\t    E001 --> E007\n72\t    E002 --> E007\n73\t    E003 --> E007\n74\t    E004 --> E007\n75\t    E005 --> E007\n76\t    E006 --> E007\n77\t\n78\t    E001 --> A008\n79\t    E002 --> A008\n80\t    E003 --> A008\n81\t    A008 --> A009\n82\t\n83\t    E001 --> B008\n84\t    E002 --> B008\n85\t    E003 --> B008\n86\t    B008 --> B009\n87\t```\n88\t\n89\tNote the deliberately absent edges: no `E004 (konflux) → deployment epics` edge\n90\tand no `deployment → E004` edge (Rule 10 — konflux onboarding runs in parallel\n91\twith general implementation; the coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline\n92\tgreen / productized image digests available\" acceptance criterion on the\n93\tdeployment epics, never by a DAG dependency). The image digests consumed by\n94\tdeployment are configuration references, not build-against artifacts (Rule 13).\n95\t\n96\t## DAG Justification\n97\t\n98\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n99\t|------|------|-----------|\n100\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | `repo-onboarding` → `konflux-onboarding` always serial; the pipeline needs the repo. |\n101\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | `license-validation` → general implementation serial; if Feast SDK transitive licenses fail, the workbench image contents change. |\n102\t| E001 → E006 | Rule 3 | Topology decision determines the CR/endpoint surface the Dashboard integration reads; true gate (`rewrite`: integration shape changes with the outcome). |\n103\t| E001/E002/E003/E004/E005/E006 → E007 | Rule 11 (+ gate) | `docs-authoring` blocked by ALL Implementation epics — docs describe what was built; also gated on the topology decision (E001) so content matches the selected branch. Docs edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs priority derived from strategy priority: Major → P1). |\n104\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E008 / BRANCH-B-E008 | Rule 3 | Investigation selects the branch; bounded outcomes (2) → conditional branches. True gate (`remove`: the non-selected branch's deployment epic does not exist). |\n105\t| E002 → BRANCH-A/B-E008 | Rule 6 | Code needs the repo; does not block other repos. |\n106\t| E003 → BRANCH-A/B-E008 | Rule 9 | If licenses fail, dependencies change and the deployment approach is affected. |\n107\t| BRANCH-A-E008 → BRANCH-A-E009 | Rule 13 | Platform Operator enablement builds against the deployment artifact the Feature Store epic produces (operator CR / server deployment); consuming Implementation is serial. |\n108\t| BRANCH-B-E008 → BRANCH-B-E009 | Rule 13 | Same as above for the standalone topology. |\n109\t| (no edge) E004 ∥ BRANCH-A/B-E008 | Rule 10 | Build config is independent of deployment code; AC-gated (build pipeline green, digests available). |\n110\t| (no edge) E002 ∥ E003 | Rule 7 | Repo onboarding and license scanning have independent inputs; parallel start. |\n111\t| (no edge) E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 8 | Konflux config doesn't depend on specific deps. |\n112\t| (no edge) E005, E006 ∥ E002/E004 | Rule 14/15 | Different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n113\t| (no edge) main-plan epics → branch epics | Branch rule | Main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics; anything depending on a specific branch's work lives inside that branch. |\n114\t\n115\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n116\t\n117\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epics |\n118\t|-----|----------|------------------------|-------|\n119\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Supported Feature Store (Feast) enabled via Platform Operator with productized images | E001, E002, E003, E004, BRANCH-A-E008, BRANCH-A-E009, BRANCH-B-E008, BRANCH-B-E009 |\n120\t| HLR-2 | P1 | Feast SDK preinstalled in at least one supported workbench image | E003 (license gate), E005 |\n121\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Dashboard shows Feature Store as enabled component with per-project endpoint links | E001 (gate), E006 |\n122\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Product documentation: enablement, getting-started, supported limits | E007 |\n123\t\n124\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. Priority inheritance: E002, E003,\n125\tE004 and the branch deployment/enablement epics are P0 because they transitively\n126\tenable HLR-1 (P0). E005 → P1 (HLR-2), E006 → P1 (HLR-3). E007 is a\n127\t`docs-authoring` epic: exempt from priority inheritance; derived from strategy\n128\tfrontmatter priority Major → P1 (see Health Warnings).\n129\t\n130\t## Component Mapping Notes\n131\t\n132\t- All strategy-listed components (Feature Store, Dashboard, Platform Operator,\n133\t  Documentation) exist in `.context/rhai-components.txt` — no non-obvious mapping\n134\t  was needed.\n135\t- **Notebooks** was added as an affected component for HLR-2 (workbench images\n136\t  are the Notebooks component's surface); it is in the canonical list.\n137\t- Feature Store has **no architecture context file** → treated as a new\n138\t  component → onboarding chain generated per Rule 20: `repo-onboarding` +\n139\t  `license-validation` (parallel start) → `konflux-onboarding` (after\n140\t  repo-onboarding) → general implementation (after license-validation, parallel\n141\t  with konflux-onboarding).\n142\t- Dashboard is the only component with an architecture context file\n143\t  (dashboard.md): integration follows the per-component feature-flag /\n144\t  OdhDashboardConfig CR pattern documented there; the Dashboard epic cites it\n145\t  (Signal 9).\n146\t\n147\t## Health Warnings\n148\t\n149\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n150\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n151\t  Non-Functional Requirements section. Team assignments were inferred from\n152\t  component ownership (RHOAI Dashboard confirmed by dashboard.md; RHOAI Feature\n153\t  Store, RHOAI Platform Operator, RHOAI Notebooks, RHOAI Documentation are\n154\t  inferred names — verify with the strategy owner). Epic acceptance criteria\n155\t  were derived from the HLRs and problem statement.\n156\t- **Docs priority vs. HLR priority**: E007 is P1 because the `docs-authoring`\n157\t  priority exception derives it from the strategy-level priority (Major → P1),\n158\t  even though HLR-4 is P2. This is rule-derived, not an inconsistency, but\n159\t  planners should not read it as documentation being more urgent than the P2\n160\t  HLR suggests.\n161\t- **Scope trap — offline store**: \"Managed offline-store infrastructure\" is\n162\t  explicitly out of scope (customers bring their own storage). No epic\n163\t  provisions offline-store infrastructure; the documentation epic must state\n164\t  this as a supported limit. Any later request to add managed offline storage\n165\t  is new strategy work, not scope creep in these epics.\n166\t- **Scope trap — Dashboard UI**: the Dashboard epic is link-out only (no\n167\t  feature-authoring UI), matching the out-of-scope statement.\n168\t- **License risk**: Feast's transitive dependency tree is unscanned; the\n169\t  license-validation epic gates both the deployment implementation and the\n170\t  workbench SDK image, so a failure there rewrites downstream scope rather\n171\t  than being discovered late.\n172\t\n173\t## Tiered Delivery\n174\t\n175\tNot applicable. Feast is brought in via a midstream fork under opendatahub-io —\n176\twe control the timing and there is no external acceptance (upstream PR/RFC or\n177\tvendor) gating delivery. Within the main plan, independent value still streams:\n178\tthe workbench SDK image (HLR-2), Dashboard presence (HLR-3), and documentation\n179\t(HLR-4) each land independently of the deployment branch timeline once their\n180\tgates clear.\n181\t\n182\t## Conditional Branches\n183\t\n184\tThe topology Investigation (E001) has two bounded outcomes:\n185\t\n186\t- **Branch A — operator-based deployment**: productize the Feast\n187\t  operator-based deployment (BRANCH-A-E008, Feature Store team), then enable it\n188\t  through the Platform Operator as a managed component (BRANCH-A-E009,\n189\t  Platform Operator team).\n190\t- **Branch B — standalone server per project**: productize the standalone\n191\t  per-project Feast server (BRANCH-B-E008, Feature Store team), then enable it\n192\t  through the Platform Operator (BRANCH-B-E009, Platform Operator team).\n193\t\n194\tBranch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-9006-E001` (also in their\n195\t`dependencies`), and `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` — if the other outcome\n196\tis selected, the branch's epics are dropped and the sibling branch applies. No\n197\tmain-plan epic depends on a branch epic; main-plan epics that depend on the\n198\tdecision (Dashboard, documentation) are gated on E001 itself. Branch epics are\n199\texcluded from the main-plan critical path.\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b063d6a7b8c890f3","agent_id":"a5b9aacc4d448e335","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"72f7aa8c-c073-4fd8-8023-460c61513f60","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:30:44.690Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88f5f6f1e972ded0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
