{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dfcc8df78304fc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E003\n3\ttitle: License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: license-validation\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 5\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# License validation for Feast and transitive dependencies\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tRun license scanning and validation over upstream Feast and its full\n35\ttransitive dependency tree to confirm the Feature Store component can ship as\n36\ta supported, productized RHOAI component and that the Feast SDK can be\n37\tpreinstalled in a supported workbench image. Feast is new to the platform, so\n38\tits dependency licenses have never been cleared.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Configure and run license scanning over the upstream Feast source tree and\n43\t  the container images planned for productization.\n44\t- Resolve the complete transitive dependency tree (including Python\n45\t  dependencies of the Feast SDK destined for workbench images) and check every\n46\t  dependency license against Red Hat's supported-license policy.\n47\t- Produce a license clearance report listing all dependencies, their licenses,\n48\t  and the disposition (approved, needs-review, blocked).\n49\t- For any needs-review or blocked dependency, document the finding and the\n50\t  mitigation options (version bump, exclusion, upstream change, or redesign of\n51\t  the productization approach).\n52\t\n53\tOut of scope: choosing the deployment topology and any deployment code — this\n54\tepic validates the software being shipped, not how it is deployed.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A license scan report exists covering upstream Feast and its transitive\n59\t  dependencies for both the container image and the workbench SDK surface.\n60\t- Every dependency has an explicit disposition; no unresolved findings remain,\n61\t  or each open finding has a documented owner and mitigation plan accepted by\n62\t  the owning teams.\n63\t- The clearance decision is recorded: Feast's dependency tree is shippable, or\n64\t  the specific blockers and required approach changes are documented for the\n65\t  downstream productization and workbench image work.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-1 (P0): productized, supported images require a cleared license profile.\n70\t- HLR-2 (P1): preinstalling the Feast SDK in a supported workbench image\n71\t  requires its transitive licenses to be cleared.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b063d6a7b8c890f3","agent_id":"a5b9aacc4d448e335","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"163b7165-5668-45f4-82fc-70fa9a049ca0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:30:54.714Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0dfcc8df78304fc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
