{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd9217ccf6b28597","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E004\n3\ttitle: Konflux onboarding for the Feature Store build pipeline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E002\n12\tai_signals:\n13\t  change_specificity: 1\n14\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n15\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n16\t  existing_foundation: 1\n17\t  open_questions: 1\n18\t  external_dependency: 0\n19\t  human_process_gates: -1\n20\t  repo_access: 1\n21\t  architecture_claims: 1\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Konflux onboarding for the Feature Store build pipeline\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tOnboard the Feature Store (Feast) component to Konflux so its productized\n35\tcontainer images are built, tested, and released through the standard RHOAI\n36\tbuild pipeline instead of ad-hoc builds. This is the known-recipe onboarding\n37\tof the midstream Feast repository created by the repository onboarding effort.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Add the Konflux application and component configuration for the midstream\n42\t  Feast repository (build root, Dockerfiles, image name/namespace conventions\n43\t  matching other RHOAI components).\n44\t- Configure the build and test pipelines per the established Konflux\n45\t  onboarding recipe for RHOAI components.\n46\t- Ensure release imagery flows to the expected registry locations so\n47\t  downstream consumers (deployment manifests, Platform Operator enablement,\n48\t  workbench images) can reference productized digests.\n49\t- Record the build pipeline status and any deviations from the standard\n50\t  recipe.\n51\t\n52\tOut of scope: deployment code, Platform Operator integration, and license\n53\tscanning — each is tracked separately and runs in parallel with this work.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The Konflux application and components for Feast exist and are active.\n58\t- The build pipeline produces a container image from the midstream repository\n59\t  and the pipeline status is green.\n60\t- Productized image digests are published to the expected registry location.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"supported ... with productized images\" — the build pipeline is\n65\t  what produces and releases those images.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b063d6a7b8c890f3","agent_id":"a5b9aacc4d448e335","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"6b137eaf-08f6-4429-ad05-33dcd75a08a0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:30:55.660Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd9217ccf6b28597","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
