 other managed components.\n50\t- Administrator enablement: the component can be enabled/disabled through the\n51\t  Platform Operator, with the deployment lifecycle (install, upgrade, removal)\n52\t  managed accordingly.\n53\t- Reference the productized image digests for the operator-based deployment\n54\t  as configuration (digests available as an acceptance gate, not a build-time\n55\t  blocking dependency).\n56\t- Handle disablement cleanly: turning the component off removes the managed\n57\t  deployment without damaging customer data in customer-managed offline\n58\t  stores.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- An administrator can enable the Feature Store through the Platform Operator\n63\t  and the operator-based deployment is installed and becomes functional;\n64\t  disabling it removes the managed deployment.\n65\t- The enablement follows the Platform Operator's established pattern for\n66\t  managed components.\n67\t- Productized image digests for the operator-based deployment are available\n68\t  and referenced in the operator configuration at execution time.\n69\t- Upgrade of the component through the Platform Operator works for at least\n70\t  one version step.\n71\t- Customer data in customer-managed offline stores survives enable/disable\n72\t  cycles.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast)\n77\t  through the Platform Operator like any other managed component, with\n78\t  productized images.\"\n79\t\n80\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n81\t\n82\t- Requires the operator-based deployment productization (its CRs and\n83\t  lifecycle surface) to exist and be stable before the operator integration\n84\t  can build against it.\n85\t- Applies only if the topology investigation selects the operator-based\n86\t  topology; otherwise this epic is removed.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b063d6a7b8c890f3","agent_id":"a5b9aacc4d448e335","session_id":"ad59e9b5-0