d components.\n51\t- Administrator enablement: the component can be enabled/disabled through the\n52\t  Platform Operator, with the per-project server lifecycle (install, upgrade,\n53\t  removal) managed accordingly.\n54\t- Reference the productized image digest for the standalone server as\n55\t  configuration (digest available as an acceptance gate, not a build-time\n56\t  blocking dependency).\n57\t- Handle disablement cleanly: turning the component off removes the managed\n58\t  deployment without damaging customer data in customer-managed offline\n59\t  stores.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- An administrator can enable the Feature Store through the Platform Operator\n64\t  and the per-project server deployment is installed and becomes functional;\n65\t  disabling it removes the managed deployment.\n66\t- The enablement follows the Platform Operator's established pattern for\n67\t  managed components.\n68\t- The productized image digest for the standalone server is available and\n69\t  referenced in the operator configuration at execution time.\n70\t- Upgrade of the component through the Platform Operator works for at least\n71\t  one version step.\n72\t- Customer data in customer-managed offline stores survives enable/disable\n73\t  cycles.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast)\n78\t  through the Platform Operator like any other managed component, with\n79\t  productized images.\"\n80\t\n81\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n82\t\n83\t- Requires the standalone per-project deployment productization (its\n84\t  deployment surface) to exist and be stable before the operator integration\n85\t  can build against it.\n86\t- Applies only if the topology investigation selects the standalone\n87\t  per-project topology; otherwise this epic is removed.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b063d6a7b8c890f3","agent_id":"a5b9aacc4d448e335","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0