{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af4536f2c4c9ef72","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Select and validate the Feast productization deployment topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Select and validate the Feast productization deployment topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the strategy's open question before any deployment or enablement work\n30\tstarts: which Feast deployment topology RHOAI productizes first — the\n31\toperator-based deployment or the standalone server per project. Upstream Feast\n32\tsupports both, but their supportability, lifecycle integration, and per-project\n33\tisolation characteristics differ. This investigation produces a documented\n34\tdecision with evidence, so that the deployment implementation and the Platform\n35\tOperator enablement work can be scoped to exactly one topology, and so the\n36\tDashboard integration knows which resource and endpoint surface to read.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Analyze both upstream Feast deployment topologies (operator-based deployment;\n41\t  standalone server per project) against product requirements: lifecycle\n42\t  management through the Platform Operator, per-project isolation, support\n43\t  burden, upgrade path, and alignment with how other managed RHOAI components\n44\t  are deployed.\n45\t- Evaluate supportability of each topology in a productized context (failure\n46\t  modes, observability, security posture, compatibility with\n47\t  customer-managed offline stores, since managed offline-store infrastructure\n48\t  is out of scope).\n49\t- Recommend one topology to productize first, with a documented rationale and\n50\t  the consequences for downstream work (deployment manifests, Platform\n51\t  Operator enablement surface, Dashboard resource/endpoint surface).\n52\t- Identify any prerequisite or follow-up work the selected topology implies\n53\t  that is not already covered by the midstream repository, build pipeline, and\n54\t  license validation efforts.\n55\t\n56\tDeliverable: a decision document recording the selected topology, the evidence,\n57\tand the consequences for the deployment, enablement, and Dashboard\n58\tintegrations.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- The decision document enumerates both candidate topologies and evaluates\n63\t  each against lifecycle integration via the Platform Operator, per-project\n64\t  isolation, support burden, and upgrade path.\n65\t- One topology is recommended with a recorded rationale and sign-off from the\n66\t  owning teams (Feature Store and Platform Operator).\n67\t- The consequences for downstream work are documented: the deployment surface\n68\t  the Feature Store team must productize, the enablement surface the Platform\n69\t  Operator team must integrate, and the resource/endpoint surface the\n70\t  Dashboard integration must read.\n71\t- Any prerequisite or follow-up work implied by the selected topology is\n72\t  identified and either confirmed as covered by existing work in this\n73\t  strategy or flagged for the strategy owner.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): the chosen topology determines how the supported Feature Store\n78\t  is deployed and enabled through the Platform Operator.\n79\t- HLR-3 (P1): the chosen topology determines the endpoint/resource surface the\n80\t  Dashboard integration presents per project.\n81\t\n82\t## Open Questions (resolved by this epic)\n83\t\n84\tThis epic is the resolution of the strategy's open question 1: \"Which Feast\n85\tdeployment topology do we productize first — the operator-based deployment or\n86\tthe standalone server per project?\"\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd","agent_id":"ab358d42db6678f9b","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"6b761bb1-053e-48fc-bc86-3ca1e0eba5d1","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:36:31.956Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af4536f2c4c9ef72","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
