{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b73de0efa7cf465d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E002\n3\ttitle: Midstream Feast repository onboarding under opendatahub-io\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: repo-onboarding\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Midstream Feast repository onboarding under opendatahub-io\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tCreate the productized midstream repository for the Feature Store (Feast)\n34\tcomponent under opendatahub-io, giving the component a home for productization\n35\tcode, downstream patches, and release automation — the foundation for its build\n36\tpipeline and deployment implementation. Today Feast is self-managed by\n37\tcustomers from upstream with no productized repository at all.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Create the midstream fork/repository for Feast under opendatahub-io following\n42\t  the established midstream onboarding recipe (branch structure, CI triggers,\n43\t  OWNERS, contribution and backport policies).\n44\t- Establish the sync/rebase workflow against the upstream Feast repository.\n45\t- Import the upstream source at the release baseline selected for\n46\t  productization and record the baseline choice.\n47\t- Wire repository-level conventions (commit standards, release tagging) to\n48\t  match other opendatahub-io component repositories.\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: container image builds and pipeline configuration (handled by\n51\tthe Konflux onboarding effort), license scanning (a parallel effort), and any\n52\tdeployment code or operator integration.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A midstream Feast repository exists under opendatahub-io with the documented\n57\t  branch structure and conventions matching other RHOAI component midstreams.\n58\t- The upstream baseline import is recorded and reproducible; the sync workflow\n59\t  against upstream is documented and executable.\n60\t- Repository OWNERS and access are configured for the Feature Store owning\n61\t  team.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-1 (P0): productized, supported images require a productized repository\n66\t  to build from.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd","agent_id":"ab358d42db6678f9b","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"451792ba-d7e7-4196-a002-e4dcba365896","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:36:39.205Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b73de0efa7cf465d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
