{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad6c15bd5d907168","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E006\n3\ttitle: Dashboard presence and endpoint links for the Feature Store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the topology decision changes the CR/endpoint surface, rewrite\n15\t    the Dashboard integration to read the selected topology's resources before merging.\n16\tai_signals:\n17\t  change_specificity: 0\n18\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n19\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n20\t  existing_foundation: 1\n21\t  open_questions: -1\n22\t  external_dependency: 0\n23\t  human_process_gates: 0\n24\t  repo_access: 1\n25\t  architecture_claims: 1\n26\timplementation_type: null\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tai_implementability: High\n29\tai_implementability_score: 4\n30\tjira_key: null\n31\tbranch: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Dashboard presence and endpoint links for the Feature Store\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tShow the Feature Store as an enabled component in the RHOAI Dashboard and link\n38\tusers to its endpoints per project. This is a link-out integration only — the\n39\tout-of-scope statement excludes a feature-authoring UI in the Dashboard for\n40\tthis release. Per the Dashboard architecture context\n41\t(rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md), the Dashboard integrates components via Kubernetes\n42\tCRs and per-component feature flags/defaults through the OdhDashboardConfig\n43\tCR; it owns no data plane.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Add Dashboard presence for the Feature Store component: it appears as an\n48\t  enabled component when the platform has it enabled, following the\n49\t  per-component feature-flag/defaults pattern in the OdhDashboardConfig CR.\n50\t- Surface per-project links to the Feature Store endpoints for projects where\n51\t  the component is enabled (link-out only; no feature-authoring UI).\n52\t- Read the component's resource/endpoint surface from the Kubernetes API\n53\t  consistent with the deployment topology selected for productization (the\n54\t  Dashboard reads CRs; it owns no data plane).\n55\t- Cover the integration with the Dashboard's existing test conventions.\n56\t\n57\tOut of scope: feature-authoring UI in the Dashboard, and any feature store\n58\tdeployment or enablement logic — the Dashboard reads what the platform\n59\tdeploys.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- When the Feature Store is enabled on the platform, the Dashboard shows it as\n64\t  an enabled component; when disabled, it is not shown.\n65\t- For each project where the component is enabled, the Dashboard links users\n66\t  to that project's Feature Store endpoints.\n67\t- The integration follows the OdhDashboardConfig feature-flag/defaults pattern\n68\t  used by other components, per the Dashboard architecture context.\n69\t- Dashboard test suite covers the new presence and link behavior.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-3 (P1): \"The Dashboard shows the Feature Store as an enabled component\n74\t  and links users to its endpoints per project.\"\n75\t\n76\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n77\t\n78\t- The deployment topology decision (operator-based vs. standalone server per\n79\t  project) must be resolved first: it determines the CR/endpoint surface this\n80\t  integration reads. The integration approach is rewritten if the topology\n81\t  decision changes it.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd","agent_id":"ab358d42db6678f9b","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0-9f8c-0292979aa557","uuid":"7067cfae-d2ad-478b-855d-2fc38cf49a48","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:36:52.026Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad6c15bd5d907168","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config",