{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-934d6713b13f525e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, operator topology (Branch A)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E008\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the topology investigation selects the standalone per-project\n17\t    topology instead, this epic is removed and the standalone enablement branch applies.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, operator topology (Branch A)\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tEnable the Feature Store (Feast) through the Platform Operator like any other\n39\tmanaged RHOAI component, for the operator-based deployment topology:\n40\tadministrators toggle the component on and the platform deploys and manages\n41\tit. This branch epic applies only if the topology investigation selects the\n42\toperator-based topology; it consumes the integration surface (operator CRs\n43\tand lifecycle) produced by the operator-based deployment productization.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Add Feature Store to the Platform Operator's managed component set using\n48\t  the operator-based deployment's CR and lifecycle surface, following the\n49\t  pattern used by other managed components.\n50\t- Administrator enablement: the component can be enabled/disabled through the\n51\t  Platform Operator, with the deployment lifecycle (install, upgrade, removal)\n52\t  managed accordingly.\n53\t- Reference the productized image digests for the operator-based deployment\n54\t  as configuration (digests available as an acceptance gate, not a build-time\n55\t  blocking dependency).\n56\t- Handle disablement cleanly: turning the component off removes the managed\n57\t  deployment without damaging customer data in customer-managed offline\n58\t  stores.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- An administrator can enable the Feature Store through the Platform Operator\n63\t  and the operator-based deployment is installed and becomes functional;\n64\t  disabling it removes the managed deployment.\n65\t- The enablement follows the Platform Operator's established pattern for\n66\t  managed components.\n67\t- Productized image digests for the operator-based deployment are available\n68\t  and referenced in the operator configuration at execution time.\n69\t- Upgrade of the component through the Platform Operator works for at least\n70\t  one version step.\n71\t- Customer data in customer-managed offline stores survives enable/disable\n72\t  cycles.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast)\n77\t  through the Platform Operator like any other managed component, with\n78\t  productized images.\"\n79\t\n80\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n81\t\n82\t- Requires the operator-based deployment productization (its CRs and\n83\t  lifecycle surface) to exist and be stable before the operator integration\n84\t  can build against it.\n85\t- Applies only if the topology investigation selects the operator-based\n86\t  topology; otherwise this epic is removed.\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd","agent_id":"ab358d42db6678f9b","session_id":"ad59e9b5-0