\t  a Feast server scoped to a project, per the selected topology decision.\n52\t- Produce the productized container image for the server through the Feature\n53\t  Store build pipeline, consuming the productized image digest as a\n54\t  configuration reference (filled in at build time).\n55\t- Validate per-project deployment and isolation on OpenShift in the\n56\t  productized form, including integration with customer-managed offline\n57\t  stores (managed offline-store infrastructure remains out of scope).\n58\t- Define the interface the Platform Operator enablement will integrate\n59\t  against (the per-project server deployment surface) for the enablement work\n60\t  that builds on this deployment.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- The standalone Feast server deploys per project on OpenShift from the\n65\t  productized manifests and images, with per-project isolation.\n66\t- The build pipeline is green for the image this deployment consumes, with\n67\t  the productized digest referenced in the shipped configuration.\n68\t- The deployment works against a customer-provided offline store.\n69\t- The integration surface for Platform Operator enablement is documented and\n70\t  stable for the enablement work that follows.\n71\t- Deployment failure modes are documented (or link to upstream documentation)\n72\t  to the level needed for support.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast)\n77\t  ... with productized images\" — this epic produces the productized,\n78\t  standalone per-project deployment that enablement turns on.\n79\t\n80\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n81\t\n82\t- Requires the midstream Feast repository and cleared licenses before the\n83\t  deployment contents are final.\n84\t- Applies only if the topology investigation selects the standalone\n85\t  per-project topology; otherwise this epic is removed.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd"