{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87746acdc2f6338d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, standalone topology (Branch\n4\t  B)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n6\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n7\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E008\n15\tgate_failure_impact:\n16\t  action: remove\n17\t  fallback_approach: If the topology investigation selects the operator-based topology\n18\t    instead, this epic is removed and the operator enablement branch applies.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Platform Operator enablement for Feature Store, standalone topology (Branch B)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tEnable the Feature Store (Feast) through the Platform Operator like any other\n40\tmanaged RHOAI component, for the standalone per-project server topology:\n41\tadministrators toggle the component on and the platform deploys and manages a\n42\tper-project server. This branch epic applies only if the topology\n43\tinvestigation selects the standalone topology; it consumes the integration\n44\tsurface produced by the standalone per-project deployment productization.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Add Feature Store to the Platform Operator's managed component set using\n49\t  the standalone per-project deployment surface, following the pattern used\n50\t  by other managed components.\n51\t- Administrator enablement: the component can be enabled/disabled through the\n52\t  Platform Operator, with the per-project server lifecycle (install, upgrade,\n53\t  removal) managed accordingly.\n54\t- Reference the productized image digest for the standalone server as\n55\t  configuration (digest available as an acceptance gate, not a build-time\n56\t  blocking dependency).\n57\t- Handle disablement cleanly: turning the component off removes the managed\n58\t  deployment without damaging customer data in customer-managed offline\n59\t  stores.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- An administrator can enable the Feature Store through the Platform Operator\n64\t  and the per-project server deployment is installed and becomes functional;\n65\t  disabling it removes the managed deployment.\n66\t- The enablement follows the Platform Operator's established pattern for\n67\t  managed components.\n68\t- The productized image digest for the standalone server is available and\n69\t  referenced in the operator configuration at execution time.\n70\t- Upgrade of the component through the Platform Operator works for at least\n71\t  one version step.\n72\t- Customer data in customer-managed offline stores survives enable/disable\n73\t  cycles.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P0): \"Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store (Feast)\n78\t  through the Platform Operator like any other managed component, with\n79\t  productized images.\"\n80\t\n81\t## Dependencies and Constraints\n82\t\n83\t- Requires the standalone per-project deployment productization (its\n84\t  deployment surface) to exist and be stable before the operator integration\n85\t  can build against it.\n86\t- Applies only if the topology investigation selects the standalone\n87\t  per-project topology; otherwise this epic is removed.\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99844f8dcd6181fd","agent_id":"ab358d42db6678f9b","session_id":"ad59e9b5-006d-46b0